<title>SWEDEN: Astra says '96 pre-tax profit up 10 pct.</title>
<headline>Astra says '96 pre-tax profit up 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish pharmaceutical company Astra AB reported these 1996 earnings on Wednesday.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			   13,220 vs 12,061</p>
<p> Sales					38,988 vs 35,800</p>
<p> Operating profit			 12,222 vs 11,115</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	   15.33 vs 14.22</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (crowns)	     4.00 vs 3.00</p>
<p> Operating costs			  26,766 vs 24,685</p>
<p> Net financial items		     1,003 vs    950</p>
<p> Minorities			   CHARGE   5 vs 4  CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					   3,771 vs  3,297</p>
<p> Net profit				  9,449 vs  8,764</p>
<p> R&amp;D					   7,057 vs  5,784</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuters poll showed analysts expected a pre-tax profit of 13.17 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
